 "observations": [
  "The page number «207» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 92», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the right above the double rule of the first field, in two lines of their own, «C 91r, O 147r,» and «N 57v.», the letters raised (L01-L02).",
  "The page holds three fields, as p. 206 (JP2 0238): «Viginti gradus Arietis» (L03), «Viginti quinque gradus Arietis» (L15) and «Triginta gradus Arietis» (L23), the ascendant at 20°, 25° and 30° of Aries. Under each heading the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine, here named «Exagonum», «Tetragonum» and «Trigonum» (L04, L16, L24); headings and numbers in bold. The first field has the heads of the columns as on p. 206 (JP2 0238, L05-L08), with «Horoscopus» under each pair of signs and without notes (L05-L08); the second and the third field have none. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on p. 206 (JP2 0238), are a third, a half and two thirds of one number. In the second field it is the last number of the field, 151° 26′ at 30° of Virgo (L22): 50° 28.7′, 75° 43′ and 100° 57.3′, printed 50° 29′, 75° 43′ and 100° 58′ (L16). In the first field 49° 57′, 74° 56′ and 99° 54′ (L04) belong to 149° 51′ to 149° 52′, 19′ more than the 149° 32′ of the table (L14), whose thirds are 49° 50.7′, 74° 46′ and 99° 41.3′; in the third 50° 47′, 76° 10′ and 101° 33′ (L24) belong to 152° 19.5′ to 152° 21′, 23′ less than the 152° 43′ of the table (L30), whose thirds are 50° 54.3′, 76° 21.5′ and 101° 48.7′; so in the second field of p. 206 (JP2 0238, L16, L22), 147° 33′ against 147° 22′.",
  "The columns, as on p. 206 (JP2 0238). In Aries and Taurus the three fields lie within 18′, 27′ and 33′ of the oblique ascensions for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′), in the third field nowhere below them and up to 33′ above them (at 15° of Taurus); at the end of Gemini they stand 53′, 59′ and 49′ above them (69° 41′ computed; 70° 34′, 70° 40′, 70° 30′), and at the end of Virgo they reach 149° 32′, 151° 26′ and 152° 43′. In each field the end of Cancer (L14, L22, L30) stands 25′ to 28′ above the mean of its neighbours in the column, as in the second and the third field of p. 206 (JP2 0238).",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the neighbouring fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant (on p. 206, JP2 0238, the fields of 5°, 10° and 15° of Aries), and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer at 30° of Aries in the first field (note a, L14: O's 50, which the edition adopts, against C's 1; 18° 50′ lies 18′ above the oblique ascension, 18° 32′, and 18° 1′ 31′ below it, the neighbouring fields having 18° 25′ and 18° 40′), at 20° of Leo in the second (note e, L20: C's 122 against O's 132; 121° 39′ and 123° 0′ in the neighbouring fields), in the trine of the third (note f, L24: the 101° 33′ of O and N, two thirds of the number of the other two heads, against C's 100° 58′, the trine of the second field, L16) and at 10° of Virgo in the third (note g, L26: C's 37 against O's 27, the steps 3° 25′ and 3° 30′ against 3° 15′ and 3° 40′). In the trine of the second field (note b, L16) the 57 of O and N is the nearer: two thirds of 151° 26′ are 100° 57.3′. At 20° of Taurus and of Gemini in the second field (notes c and d, L20) the readings differ by 1′ (32° 54′ or 32° 53′, between 32° 35′ and 32° 59′; 59° 51′ or 59° 50′, between 59° 57′ and 59° 45′); neither is decided.",
  "Without variants: in the second field 40° 15′ at 30° of Taurus (L22) lies 14′ and 50′ below the neighbouring fields (40° 29′, 41° 5′) and 27′ below the oblique ascension, 40° 42′, between the steps 3° 32′ and 5° 7′. In the third field the steps of Virgo, 3° 25′ to 3° 37′ from the end of Leo to 20° of Virgo, fall to 3° 0′ and rise to 4° 10′ in the last two (L29-L30).",
  "The addition of C (N03-N04), in its upper margin, with the editor's question marks: «S. . . (?) elmirech (?) a zodiaco in aequinoctialem radiatio cadit mittaturque secundum latitudinem ipsius gradus», the radiation falls from the zodiac into the equator and is to be cast according to the latitude of that degree. Italics: «Addid. C in marg. superiore».",
  "The upper half of the 8 of «87» at 15° of Cancer in the second field (L19) is faint; a short stroke at the upper left of the T of «Trigonum» in L24, and specks above the 21 of Leo in L09 and after the 35 of Leo in L20; not transcribed.",
  "N03: in the additions, p. 236 (JP2 0268, L03-L13), Suter reads «S... elmirech» as «Secundum Emirethium», as in the note of Tab. 7 (p. 118, JP2 0150, N13), and refers it to the tables of Eumathius as corrected by al-Zarqālī."
